---
title: Ghee
yield: 1000%grams     # how much it makes (number%unit); lets other recipes ask for e.g. @./this{400%grams}
tags:
  - ingredient
---

Cut @butter{1300%grams} into big chunks and place in large pot over medium-low heat.

> I use a big block of 83% fat butter

Prepare a strainer and cheese cloth over a bowl or other pot.

Allow the butter to melt then simmer or slightly boil until all the water boils off.

> The milk protiens will float to the top and start to brown, while the liquid ghee will become clear and an amber color.

Once the water is boiled off take the pot off the heat and let cool.

Strain through the strainer / cheese cloth, then pour into your storage containers.

> Pint mason jars work well
